---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Frequently Asked Questions | CogniFocus";
const description =
  "Frequently asked questions about CogniFocus: Shield blocking, Manual Block, Planned Sessions, permissions, privacy, tiers, and planned features.";
const canonical = "https://cognifocus.app/faq.html";
const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What is CogniFocus?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "CogniFocus is an Android focus timer built around Shield blocking, Manual Block, Planned Sessions, Goblin reactions, and recovery nudges.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "How does Shield work during focus sessions?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "During an active session, Shield watches for blocked apps and steps in before the scroll takes over.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What is Manual Block?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Manual Block lets you block selected apps outside a focus session when you want direct protection for a specific window.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What are Planned Sessions?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Planned Sessions are focus blocks you schedule ahead of time so recurring routines are ready before work starts.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What happens if I pause or slip?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Pausing temporarily stops the session, and recovery nudges help you return if you drift into a blocked app.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "Why does CogniFocus need Android permissions?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "CogniFocus uses Usage Access to see the foreground app and Display over other apps to show Shield. It does not need those permissions to read your content.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What does CogniFocus not read?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "CogniFocus does not read your messages, contacts, passwords, or the text inside your apps.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What do Basic, Pro, and Limitless include?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Basic, or Free, covers the core focus loop with lighter limits. Pro expands the session tools with stronger Shield capacity, Manual Block, Planned Sessions, reminders, recovery nudges, and restore support. If a Limitless tier is offered later, its exact limits and extras will be listed on pricing before checkout.",
      },
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      name: "What features are planned for later?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Planned features include Ghost Mode, DND-style quieting, uninstall protection, and advanced lock rules. They are planned for later and are not all live yet.",
      },
    },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  ogImageAlt="CogniFocus FAQ page"
  bodyClass="faq-page cf-shell"
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema, null, 2)} />

  <main id="main-content" class="faq-main">
    <header class="container text-center faq-hero">
      <span class="feature-kicker">FAQ <span aria-hidden="true">&#10067;</span></span>
      <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
      <p class="faq-subtitle">Detailed answers about CogniFocus, Shield blocking, Manual Block, permissions, privacy, tiers, and planned features.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="faq-content-wrap">
      <div class="faq-content-inner">
        <section class="cf-faq-accordion mt-4">
          <article class="cf-faq-item p-3 mb-3">
            <div class="faq-card-header">
              <div class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10024;</div>
              <div>
                <h3>What is CogniFocus?</h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-faq-content">
              <p>CogniFocus is an Android focus timer built around Shield blocking, Manual Block, Planned Sessions, Goblin reactions, and recovery nudges. It is made for focus sessions that push back when attention drifts instead of just counting down.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="cf-faq-item p-3 mb-3">
            <div class="faq-card-header">
              <div class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9201;</div>
              <div>
                <h3>How does Shield work during focus sessions?</h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-faq-content">
              <p>During an active session, Shield watches for blocked apps and steps in before the scroll takes over. The Goblin reacts, and the session nudges you back toward work instead of letting the distraction loop win.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="cf-faq-item p-3 mb-3">
            <div class="faq-card-header">
              <div class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128245;</div>
              <div>
                <h3>What is Manual Block?</h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-faq-content">
              <p>Manual Block lets you block selected apps outside a focus session. Use it for study time, bedtime, or any window where you want direct protection without starting a planned session.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="cf-faq-item p-3 mb-3">
            <div class="faq-card-header">
              <div class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128274;</div>
              <div>
                <h3>What are Planned Sessions?</h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-faq-content">
              <p>Planned Sessions are focus blocks you schedule ahead of time. They are useful for recurring routines, so your focus session is ready before the day gets noisy.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="cf-faq-item p-3 mb-3">
            <div class="faq-card-header">
              <div class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#127822;</div>
              <div>
                <h3>What happens if I pause or slip?</h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-faq-content">
              <p>Pausing temporarily stops the session. If you slip into a blocked app, recovery nudges help you come back without losing the whole run. The Goblin keeps it honest, but one bad moment does not have to end the session.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="cf-faq-item p-3 mb-3">
            <div class="faq-card-header">
              <div class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128274;</div>
              <div>
                <h3>Why does it need Android permissions?</h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-faq-content">
              <p>Usage Access lets CogniFocus see which app is in front so Shield can react. Display over other apps lets the Shield screen appear. Those permissions are used for focus protection, not for reading your content.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="cf-faq-item p-3 mb-3">
            <div class="faq-card-header">
              <div class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#127822;</div>
              <div>
                <h3>What does CogniFocus not read?</h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-faq-content">
              <p>CogniFocus does not read your messages, contacts, passwords, or the text inside your apps. It uses the app-in-front signal and your session state to protect focus, not private content.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="cf-faq-item p-3 mb-3">
            <div class="faq-card-header">
              <div class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128142;</div>
              <div>
                <h3>What do Basic, Pro, and Limitless include?</h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-faq-content">
              <p>Basic, or Free, covers the core focus loop with lighter limits. Pro expands the session tools with stronger Shield capacity, Manual Block, Planned Sessions, reminders, recovery nudges, and restore support. If a Limitless tier is offered later, its exact limits and extras will be listed on pricing before checkout.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article class="cf-faq-item p-3 mb-3">
            <div class="faq-card-header">
              <div class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#10024;</div>
              <div>
                <h3>What features are planned for later?</h3>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="cf-faq-content">
              <p>Planned features include Ghost Mode, DND-style quieting, uninstall protection, and advanced lock rules. They are planned for later and are not all live yet.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
